==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing F_PermissionMatrix removes the closed-world definition of the allowed set; injecting a violation that adds Customer->PostDecision to the allowed set directly contradicts the LeastPrivilege and FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions assertions, which check that customers cannot record decisions.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_001_CustomerCanSubmit, FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_001_CustomerCanSubmit: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Clearing F_OnePendingPerCustomer removes the constraint that prevents two PendingReview applications from sharing the same owner. Injecting two distinct applications in PendingReview with the same owner forces the FR_005 assertion to find a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditSubmitEvent  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuditSubmitEvent.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditSubmitEvent allows a LoanApplication to exist with no EvSubmitted audit event. Injecting an application that has no corresponding submission event forces the AuditCompleteness and FR_016_AuditTrail assertions to fail.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditTrail
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrail: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionByStaff  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_DecisionByStaff.als
    rationale: Clearing F_DecisionByStaff allows a Customer-role User to appear as decidedBy on a Decision. Injecting such a Decision forces FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions and AttributionCorrectness to fail because they assert all decisions are made by BankStaff.
    expected to FAIL: FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions, AttributionCorrectness
      - FR_015_StaffOnlyDecisions: FAIL (expected)
      - AttributionCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_DecisionInjectivity  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_DecisionInjectivity.als
    rationale: Clearing F_DecisionInjectivity removes the constraint that a Decision object can belong to at most one LoanApplication. Injecting two distinct applications that share the same Decision atom simulates the dual-decision scenario that FR-012 forbids.
    expected to FAIL: ConcurrencySafety, FR_012_ConcurrentDecisionSafety
      - ConcurrencySafety: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_ConcurrentDecisionSafety: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditSubmitActorIsOwner  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuditSubmitActorIsOwner.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AuditSubmitActorIsOwner allows a EvSubmitted event to be attributed to a User who is not the application's owner. Injecting such a misattribution directly violates AttributionCorrectness and FR_013_CustomerSeesOwnOnly, which assert the submit-event actor is always the owning customer.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_013_CustomerSeesOwnOnly
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerSeesOwnOnly: FAIL (expected)

